BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:25th Hour
DTSTART:20260820T190000
DTEND:20260820T210000
DTSTAMP:20260820T114809Z
UID:91cdec365412e6c0b9a56a98778d6f@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Director of the Month: Spike Lee The great Spike Lee’s most 
 underrated film\, 25th Hour finds Academy Award-nominee Edward Norton lead
 ing an amazing all-star cast in this critically acclaimed film\, recognize
 d for its compassionate view of post-9/11 New York City. In 24 short hours
 \, Monty Brogan (Norton) goes to prison for a seven-year bid. Once a king 
 of Manhattan\, Monty is about to say goodbye to the life he knew\, a life 
 that opened doors to New York’s swankiest clubs but also alienated him f
 rom the people closest to him. In his last day on the outside\, Monty trie
 s to reconnect with his father (Brian Cox)\, and gets together with two ol
 d friends\, Jacob (Philip Seymour Hoffman) and Slaughtery (Barry Pepper). 
 And then there’s his girlfriend\, Naturelle (Rosario Dawson)\, who might
  (or might not) have been the one who tipped off the cops. Monty’s not s
 ure of much these days\, but with time running out\, there are choices to 
 be made as he struggles to redeem himself in the 25th hour. Every actor li
 sted here does top-notch work. David Benioff (Game of Thrones) wrote the s
 cript\, adapted from his novel. The Screening Room @VTIFF\n\nSources: Verm
 ont Public
LOCATION:60 Lake St
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/25th-hour-
 05-08-2026-11-15-55
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Animals in Myth & Legend with VINS
DTSTART:20260820T190000
DTEND:20260820T203000
DTSTAMP:20260820T114809Z
UID:7de10693cf6c8370c3c76ed142ea25@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Please join us for a free\, live animal presentation brought t
 o us by Vermont Institute of Natural Science (VINS). How did Snake lose he
 r legs? Why does Owl only fly at night? How did Turtle fly south for the w
 inter? Meet these animals and hear their stories while we learn about the 
 adaptations they have that help them survive. A VINS educator will bring u
 s on an exploration of a few different tales that people tell to help them
  understand the world of wildlife around them. Founded in 1972\, VINS is a
  leader in environmental education and wildlife conservation and care. The
 y are known nationally for innovative natural science curricula and educat
 ion programs for learners of all ages. Donations appreciated\n\nSources: V
 ermont Public
LOCATION:Brookfield Old Town Hall\, 93 Stone Road
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/animals-in
 -myth-legend-with-vins-09-08-2026-10-34-15
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bamboozled
DTSTART:20260820T190000
DTEND:20260820T211500
DTSTAMP:20260820T114809Z
UID:587e768cb7c99b5892eef053f61d28@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:With this blisteringly funny\, unapologetically confrontationa
 l satire\, writer-director Spike Lee examined the past\, present\, and fut
 ure of racism in American popular culture\, issuing a daring provocation t
 o creators and consumers alike—so on-point that it’s sometimes hard to
  watch. Bamboozled might be a bit hit-and-miss\, but the hits are devastat
 ing. Using its Producers-ish premise to horrifying effect\, Bamboozled tel
 ls the story of academic television writer Pierre Delacroix (Damon Wayans)
 \, who’s been assigned with rescuing his network’s flagging ratings. H
 is explosively offensive solution? Bring back blackface. To his horror\, t
 he white network executives love it\, and so do audiences: The New Millenn
 ium Minstrel Show is a hit\, forcing Pierre and his collaborators to confr
 ont their public’s insatiable appetite for dehumanizing stereotypes. Fea
 turing Savion Glover\, Jada Pinkett Smith\, Tommy Davidson\, Mos Def\, and
  Paul Mooney\, Bamboozled is a stinging indictment of mass entertainment a
 t the turn of the 21st century that looks more damning with each passing y
 ear.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Main Street Landing Film House\, 60 Lake St
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/bamboozled
 -11-08-2026-15-30-28
END:VEVENT
