BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summer Concert Series: Baby Fearn
DTSTART:20260821T123000
DTEND:20260821T133000
DTSTAMP:20260820T114809Z
UID:529af072775fad1fb317dbfadcdb79@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Baby Fearn has grown from her Vermont roots as a singer\, perf
 ormer\, and glitter-loving pansexual. A former musical theater kid\, she h
 as carried her passion for storytelling\, performance\, and song into an e
 volving musical career that blends pop\, jazz\, musical theatre\, soul\, a
 nd rock. Creating community is her biggest goal\, and she hopes to be able
  to not only be a part of it but create a space through her music that is 
 safe and fun for everyone. Whether she’s being playful\, flirty\, or int
 rospective\, Baby Fearn strives to spark joy in everyone in the space so c
 ome hang out and enjoy the show. A seasonal celebration of Vermont’s inc
 redible musicians\, the Summer Concert Series has been serving up a side o
 f local music to downtown Burlington at lunchtime for 14 years. Summer in 
 the City is made possible in part thanks to Underwriters at the Pomerleau 
 Family Foundation\; Supporters Burlington Telecom\, Myti\, Soundtoys\, and
  Lake Champlain Chocolates\, and Community Partner American Flatbread Burl
 ington & Mothership Brewery. Media Sponsors: Seven Days and WCAX.⁠\n\nSo
 urces: Vermont Public
LOCATION:City Hall Park\, 135 Church st
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/summer-con
 cert-series-baby-fearn-19-06-2026-20-20-42
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Four of Us
DTSTART:20260821T190000
DTEND:20260821T213000
DTSTAMP:20260820T114809Z
UID:d8b0c948b80165c5178cea198871da@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:A funny\, poignant\, and deeply moving exploration of friendsh
 ip\, The Four of Us follows two lifelong companions whose relationship is 
 forever changed when one of them finds unexpected literary success. As mem
 ories\, rivalries\, and long-held assumptions rise to the surface\, the pl
 ay examines the complicated ways ambition\, identity\, and affection inter
 twine. With Moses' signature wit and emotional insight\, The Four of Us is
  a compelling portrait of the stories we tell ourselves—and each other
 —about success\, loyalty\, and growing apart. 139 Main St #407\, Brattle
 boro\, VT 05301 \, Vermont 05301 (802) 218-3232 hookerdunhamtheater.org Su
 bmit An Event Find out what's happening in your neck of the woods with Ver
